WEBVTT

00:23:58.499 --> 00:24:00.460
and then four more who are grandparents

00:24:00.484 --> 00:24:02.386
and then 12 more who are collaborators.

00:24:02.410 --> 00:24:05.692
She built this intimate web
of connections around these kids,

00:24:05.716 --> 00:24:08.429
and in part, it was to create
structure for the kids.

00:24:08.453 --> 00:24:11.227
Somebody could drive them to school,
bring them a sandwich.

00:24:11.251 --> 00:24:13.886
But in part, it was to bond
the adults with each other.

00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:17.056
And that's one of things I noticed
about the weavers in particular.

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:19.255
It's the radical mutuality.

00:24:19.279 --> 00:24:22.023
We're all broken, we're all walking
through this together.

00:24:22.047 --> 00:24:24.157
As one of them from New Orleans told me,

00:24:24.181 --> 00:24:27.237
"We don't do things for people,
we don't things to people,

00:24:27.261 --> 00:24:28.686
we do things with people."

00:24:28.710 --> 00:24:32.574
And it's that complete sense
of social equality and moral equality